iews":93218,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1793422800000,"source":"Geoscience Australia"},{"id":"a3c0473199e248dd98212a9f57b0fc5a","owner":"jeffhuffman","created":1755286596000,"modified":1772495653000,"guid":null,"name":"National_Nexrad_Coverage_with_Population","title":"US Nexrad Radar Coverage","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Multilayer","Service","Hosted Service"],"description":"<b>Overview<\/b>  \n<p>This feature service provides spatial data on US radar coverage by the National Weather Service (NWS) and Nielsen Designated Market Area (DMA) boundaries. It integrates multiple layers encompassing radar coverage quality, media market demographics, and population statistics.<\/p>  \n\n<b>Feature Layers<\/b>  \n<ul>  \n<li><b>National Nexrad Coverage<\/b>: Represents the radar coverage areas at various heights across the United States with spatial geometry delineating coverage zones. It serves as a national overview of radar reach and effectiveness at elevation levels.<\/li>  \n<li><b>Nexrad Poor Coverage (above 4k ft)<\/b>: Highlights areas with poor radar coverage at altitudes above 4,000 feet, identifying geographic regions where radar signal strength and quality may be insufficient for comprehensive weather monitoring.<\/li>  \n<li><b>Poor Coverage by TV Market<\/b>: Combines radar coverage deficiencies with Nielsen DMA boundaries to assess poor radar performance in defined media market areas, enriched with demographic data such as population estimates and age distributions.<\/li>  \n<li><b>Nielsen DMA Boundaries<\/b>: Provides detailed boundaries for Nielsen Designated Market Areas, including demographic profiles like age, gender, and racial/ethnic composition. This layer supports contextual analysis of regions affected by radar coverage issues.<\/li>  \n<\/ul>  \n\n<b>Geographic Coverage<\/b>  \n<p>The layers collectively cover the continental United States, detailing national radar coverage and media market boundaries, allowing for integrated analysis across geographic and demographic dimensions.<\/p>  \n\n<b>Use Cases<\/b>  \n<ul>  \n<li>Assessing and planning for radar infrastructure improvements by identifying areas of poor coverage by altitude and media market.<\/li>  \n<li>Supporting broadcast and emergency management decision-making by linking radar performance with media market demographics.<\/li>  \n<li>Enabling demographic analysis within media markets to tailor communication strategies for weather-related events.<\/li>  \n<\/ul>","tags":["radar coverage","Nexrad","NWS","Nielsen DMA","media markets","population demographics","US weather monitoring","radar signal quality","broadcast regions"],"snippet":"This feature service delivers detailed US radar coverage data alongside Nielsen DMA boundaries, combining weather radar performance with demographic insights for enhanced analysis of media markets and radar infrastructure.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-171.5500018179046,10.744127277563052],[147.58090997648884,67.72528168659417]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services6.arcgis.com/LT1iWT50Endhh6TU/arcgis/rest/services/National_Nexrad_Coverage_with_Population/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":3103,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1793372400000,"source":"Baron Weather"},{"id":"3ac5e43be16b41dc92e7f24b17e71400","owner":"baron.marketing","created":1747244544000,"modified":1782113616000,"guid":null,"name":"Global_Derived_Radar","title":"Simulated Radar Mosaic (Global)","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p><b>Time:<\/b> Current&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Updates:<\/b> 15 min<br /><b>Resolution:<\/b> 4 km&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Units:<\/b> dBZ&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Coverage:<\/b> Global<\/p><p>Utilizing global satellite data and processing that simulates radar reflectivity from the satellite data, Global Derived Radar is particularly useful because it provides \"synthetic radar data\" for areas not covered by traditional land-based radar, making it particularly useful in identifying storms developing offshore, such as cyclones and hurricanes. The additional \"minus CONUS\" product provides a complete view of precipitation occurring worldwide, but with the Continental U.S. removed, allowing developers to display a more detailed radar product for the U.S. while using the satellite-derived radar everywhere else on the globe; the Max Reflectivity-based Standard Radar (2.5-Minute Updates) is the recommended product for this instance.<\/p><p><b>Industries<\/b> best served by this data include: Government and Global, Aviation, XMWX Satellite.<\/p>","tags":["Everyday Weather","Global","Premium","Radar Composites","Sample","v2"],"snippet":"A world view of a simulated radar from advanced satellite processing.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-179.99998854118687,-64.74509999985698],[179.99998854118684,64.92066999997287]],"categories":["/Categories/National Government","/Categories/Aviation"],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services6.arcgis.com/LT1iWT50Endhh6TU/arcgis/rest/services/Global_Derived_Radar/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":["Government and Global","Aviation","XMWX Satellite"],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":11890,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1793422800000,"source":"Baron Weather"},{"id":"ad4d6695a66f49b2b55a03cad2716bc6","owner":"baron.marketing","created":1747257455000,"modified":1782113573000,"guid":null,"name":"North_American_Radar","title":"North American Radar","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p><b>Time:<\/b> Current&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Updates:<\/b> 2 min<br /><b>Resolution:<\/b> 1 km&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Units:<\/b> dBZ&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Coverage:<\/b> United States<\/p><p>The best data product to use for a complete radar view of the entire United States. This is a mosaic image of radars covering the continental US, Alaska, Hawaii, Puerto Rico, and the southern portion of Canada. A high 1km resolution combined with 2-minute updates make High-Res North American Radar an advantageous mix of weather radar detail and timeliness. This product is very useful for applications requiring seamless radar coverage throughout the United States, Puerto Rico and southern portions of Canada.<\/p><p><b>Industries<\/b> best served by this data include: Government and Global, Maritime, Media, Public Safety, Transportation, XMWX Satellite, Aviation.<\/p>","tags":["Advanced","Everyday Weather","Radar Composites","Sample","United States","v2"],"snippet":"The highest-resolution composite radar in the industry, eliminating clutter and updating every two minutes.","thumbnail":"thumbnai