dar. Cada entidad está identificada por un identificador único y se acompaña de atributos descriptivos como el nombre de la cobertura, la ruta asociada en el sistema de archivos, y medidas geométricas cuantitativas de área y perímetro. Estas características permiten evaluar el alcance y la dimensión espacial de las coberturas radar.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<b>Aplicaciones Potenciales<\/b>\n<ul>\n<li>Planificación y administración de sistemas de detección radar.<\/li>\n<li>Monitoreo de cobertura para operaciones de seguridad, meteorología o control aéreo.<\/li>\n<li>Integración en sistemas GIS para análisis espacial avanzado y visualización de coberturas.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","tags":["cobertura radar","zona andina","polígonos geoespaciales","áreas radar","medidas geográficas"],"snippet":"Servicio de datos que muestra las áreas de cobertura radar en regiones andinas, facilitando análisis espacial y planificación operativa.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-83.85869999999994,-18.511999999999944],[-68.89499999999998,-1.3871999999999503]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"4326","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"es-ec","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services9.arcgis.com/D3h5nfeJruznFVd8/arcgis/rest/services/COBERTURAS_RADAR/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":422,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1793401200000},{"id":"ae5b88ab92c64bbc88127a5fff61c48a","owner":"vagomez_cob","created":1701370332000,"modified":1792532026000,"guid":null,"name":"Radar_Feedback_view","title":"Radar Feedback","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service","View Service"],"description":"<font color='#000000' face='Times New Roman, Times New Roman_EmbeddedFont, Times New Roman_MSFontService, serif'><span style='font-size:16px;'>This data shows the street where radar feedback is projected to be built along with its status, date of completion, <\/span><\/font><div>and its boundaries. <\/div><div><br /><\/div>","tags":["Public Works","Safe Routes","Schools","Radar Feedback"],"snippet":"This layer represents the one of various infrastructure improvements to school transportation corridors that the City of Bakersfield\u2019s Public Works Department has implemented or plans to implement. A radar speed sign is an interactive sign that displays vehicle speed as motorists approach. The purpose of radar speed signs is to slow cars down by making drivers aware when they are driving at speeds above the posted limits.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1706307335960.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-119.07342371351324,35.30315448941912],[-118.9482317358938,35.40961749078464]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Public Works. Current editor is Valerie Saenz","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><div style='margin-bottom:3rem;'><div><div style='padding-bottom:0.375rem; max-width:100%; display:inherit;'><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem;'><span style='font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size:12pt;'>Does not replace official recorded documents. Contact Public Works for more information.<\/span><\/p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px;'><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div>","culture":"","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services3.arcgis.com/OKildAHLkXjQX8Ca/arcgis/rest/services/Radar_Feedback_view/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2861,"scoreCompleteness":95,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1793412000000,"source":"City of Bakersfield","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"d6387fcd0e7046189ef263143c641d8e","owner":"user_semillero","created":1781669505000,"modified":1781819690000,"guid":null,"name":"RADARES","title":"Capas de Radares en la Región Andina","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Public Data Collection","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<b>Descripción general<\/b> <p>Este servicio presenta una capa geográfica dedicada a la localización y características de radares en una zona específica de la región andina. La capa denominada <strong>RADARES<\/strong> incluye datos que permiten identificar cada radar mediante su nombre y su ubicación organizada en rutas o carpetas, lo que facilita su administración y consulta.<\/p><p>El servicio utiliza un sistema de referencia espacial estándar para asegurar la compatibilidad con diversas herramientas SIG y proporciona información clave para análisis de cobertura y planificación en sectores como seguridad, meteorología o gestion territorial.<\/p><b>Capas incluidas<\/b> <ul><li><strong>RADARES<\/strong>: capa de entidades geoespaciales que contiene puntos que representan estaciones de radar. Cada entidad cuenta con un identificador único y atributos descriptivos para apoyar la visualización y presentación de información en mapas interactivos.<\/li><\/ul><b>Cobertura geográfica<\/b> <p>El área cubierta abarca una porción del territorio andino, que incluye regiones dentro de los países ubicados entre aproximadamente las latitudes -16.48 y -3.61, y longitudes -81.22 a -71.06, abarcando principalmente áreas montañosas y sus alrededores.<\/p><b>Usos potenciales<\/b> <ul><li>Monitoreo de radar para aplicaciones meteorológicas y de vigilancia.<\/li><li>Planificación de infraestructura y logística en zonas de difícil acceso.<\/li><li>Visualización y análisis espacial en sistemas de información geográfica para la gestión pública y privada.<\/li><\/ul>","tags":["radares","región andina","estaciones meteorológicas","geolocalización","infraestructura tecnológica"],"snippet":"Servicio con capa de radares que localiza y describe estaciones de radar en una zona específica de la región andina, útil para monitoreo y análisis geoespacial.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-81.22590599961998,-16.480138999855736],[-71.0590000001866,-3.6127779998638054]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"es-ec","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services9.arcgis.com/D3h5nfeJruznFVd8/arcgis/rest/services/RADARES/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":434,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1793397600000},{"id":"228b1584b89a45308ed4256c5bedd43d","owner":"CM_3RWW","created":1541611083000,"modified":1757526961000,"guid":null,"name":"garrd","title":"Gauge Adjusted Radar Rainfall Data Geometry","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Multilayer","Service","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div>This service contains the locations used for 3RWW's Gauge-Adjusted Radar Rainfall Data (GARRD) services.\n\nGARRD is also referred to as Calibrated Radar Rainfall Data.<\/div><div><br /><\/div><div><span style='font-weight: bold;'>Note: <\/span>this layer doesn't contain any rainfall data; it only provides the locations for which gauge adjusted radard rainfall data is produced.<\/div><div><br /><\/div><div>More information is available on <a href='http://www.3riverswetweather.org/municipalities/calibrated-radar-rainfall-data' target='_blank'>http://www.3riverswetweather.org/municipalities/calibrated-radar-rainfall-data<\/a><\/div>","tags":["rain"," weather"," rainfall"," radar"," gauge"," calibrated"," NOAA"," 3RWW"," Pittsburgh"," Allegheny County"],"snippet":"Geometry for 3RWW's Gauge-Adjusted Radar Rainfall Data. Note: this layer doesn't contain any rainfall data.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-80.38301029408888,40.17179474527211],[-79.65880133083189,40.698841244840295]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102729","accessInformation":"3RWW, Vieux Associates, CivicMapper, Teragon, ALCOSAN","classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services6.arcgis.com/dMKWX9NPCcfmaZl3/arcgis/rest/services/garrd/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":19123,"scoreCompleteness":80,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1793422800000,"source":"3 Rivers Wet Weather"},{"id":"e0f2b264bf1849c2bc6d1526c581f131","owner":"MBaker@parametrix.com_uplan","created":1701284561000,"modified":1792007528000,"guid":null,"name":"SideFireRadarLocations","title":"UDOT Planning - SideFire Radar Locations 2024","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>This feature service includes the approximate locations of Side Fire Radar sensors. The estimated locations were derived based on a PeMS output and using ALRS. The layer was developed as a part of the Active Transportation Count Program study. There are no plans for it to be updated.<\/span>","tags":["UDOT","Planning","Side Fire","Radar","Point","AT","Data Collection","Data","Count","Active Transportation"],"snippet":"This feature service includes the approximate locations of Side Fire Radar sensors. The estimated locations were derived based on a PeMS output and using ALRS. The layer was developed as a part of the Active Transportation Count Program study. There are no plans for it to be updated. ","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1737581769074.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-113.79874445192961,37.07474039488231],[-109.4654679437313,41.996617664479295]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"26912","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p style='font-weight:bold;'>This data is for informational purposes and must be field verified prior to being used on a project.<\/p><p>UDOT makes no warranty with respect to the accuracy, completeness or usefulness of this content or consequential damages resulting from the use or misuse of the content or any of the information contained herein. Please contact the UDOT GIS Department at <a href='mailto:udotgis@utah.gov' rel='nofollow ugc'>udotgis@utah.gov<\/a> for more information.<\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/pA2nEVnB6tquxgOW/arcgis/rest/services/SideFireRadarLocations/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":412,"scoreCompleteness":96,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1793394000000,"source":"UPlan Map Center"},{"id":"b9c527e0cb6d4c7fac39981f966fdd65","owner":"ncei_noaa","created":1593473861000,"modified":1688431342000,"guid":null,"name":"NEXRAD_Stations","title":"NEXRAD Stations","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Build a layer","Collector","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Feature Service Template","General","Layer","Layer Template","Platform","Service","Service template","Singlelayer","Template","Hosted Service"],"description":"<span style='color:rgb(68, 68, 68); font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13.5541px;'>NEXRAD is a network of 160 high-resolution Doppler weather radars operated by the NOAA National Weather Service (NWS), the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA), and the U.S. Air Force (USAF). Doppler radars detect atmospheric precipitation and winds, which allow scientists to track and anticipate weather events, such as rain, ice pellets, snow, hail, and tornadoes, as well as some non-weather objects like birds and insects. NEXRAD stations use the Weather Surveillance Radar - 1988, Doppler (WSR-88D) system. The NEXRAD products are divided in two data processing levels. The lower Level 2 data are base products at original resolution. Level 2 data are recorded at all NWS and most USAF and FAA WSR-88D sites. From the Level 2 quantities, computer processing generates numerous meteorological analysis Level 3 products. The Level 3 data consists of reduced resolution, low-bandwidth, base products as well as many derived, post-processed products. Level 3 products are recorded at most U.S. sites, though non-US sites do not have Level 3 products. There are over 40 Level 3 products available from the NCDC. General products for Level 3 include the base and composite reflectivity, storm relative velocity, vertical integrated liquid, echo tops and VAD wind profile. Precipitation products for Level 3 include estimated ground accumulated rainfall amounts for one and three hour periods, storm totals, and digital arrays. Estimates are based on reflectivity to rainfall rate (Z-R) relationships. Overlay products for Level 3 are alphanumeric data that give detailed information on certain parameters for an identified storm cell. These include storm structure, hail index, mesocyclone identification, tornadic vortex signature, and storm tracking information. Radar messages for Level 3 are sent by the radar site to users in order to know more about the radar status and special product data. NEXRAD data are provided to the NOAA National Climatic Data Center for archiving and dissemination to users. Data coverage varies by station and ranges from May 1992 to 1 day from present. Most stations began observing in the mid-1990s, and most period of records are continuous.<\/span><div><a href='https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/maps/radar/' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Map<\/a><br /><\/div><div><a href='https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/search/data-search/weather-radar-level-ii' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Data<\/a><span style='color:rgb(68, 68, 68); font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13.5541px;'><br /><\/span><\/div>","tags":["Data Collection","radar","weather events","Doppler"],"snippet":"This dataset consists of Level II and Level III weather radar data collected from Next-Generation Radar (NEXRAD) stations located in the contiguous United States, Alaska, Hawaii, U.S. territories and at military base sites.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1594903656417.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-179.99999999999696,-88.77194000000019],[179.99999999999696,84.99999999999855]],"categories":["/Categories/Feature Layers"],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI).","classification":null,"licenseInfo