ng analysis of vehicle speeds, traffic volumes, and behavioral patterns across monitored locations. The dataset is the result of a structured data processing pipeline that includes extraction, validation, deduplication, and aggregation of sensor data.<\/p><p>This layer is intended to replace the legacy traffic data dashboard dataset and serves as the authoritative source for all traffic-related visualizations, reporting, and decision-making tools. It enables City staff to monitor traffic trends, identify speeding concerns, evaluate safety conditions, and support data-driven infrastructure and enforcement strategies.<\/p><p>The dataset is designed for ongoing updates as new Radar and RU2 data are processed and appended. It integrates seamlessly with dashboards, maps, and analytical workflows, providing a consistent and reliable foundation for traffic monitoring.<\/p><p>Users should treat this layer as the single source of truth for processed traffic data and avoid maintaining separate or duplicate datasets. All updates should follow the established processing pipeline to ensure data consistency and integrity.<\/p>","tags":["Radar","Ru2","Traffic Dashboard","data"],"snippet":"Traffic data map that contains the Radar and Ru2 processed data with 85% included. This is to replace the current version of the traffic data dashboard. ","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1773954494117.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-111.52174245378319,40.64003548269036],[-111.46207826953027,40.67557836784335]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p>The information on this page is provided \u201cas is,\u201d with no guarantees relating to the availability, completeness, or accuracy of the data. &nbsp;This information is provided as a public service for informational purposes only. You are solely responsible and assume all risk for your use of the information. Park City reserves the right to change, revise, or discontinue published data.<\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/wmY050uFnMPcgSCc/arcgis/rest/services/Traffic_Data_Map_WFL1/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2055,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1793386800000,"source":"Park City Municipal Corp.","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"d3b5934d25a448bf8517e4f2ff094213","owner":"john.carpenter@ncwildlife.gov","created":1489521181000,"modified":1764183226000,"guid":null,"name":"NEXRAD_Spring","title":"NEXRAD_Spring","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Multilayer","Service","Hosted Service"],"description":"For each suitable radar sampling day, we used instantaneous measures of vertically-integrated radar reflectivity (VIR); the relative emigrant density in the air from the ground to 1.5 km above ground) interpolated in time to the peak of bird nocturnal flight exodus to map relative emigrant bird stopover densities. We classified bird stopover use by the seasonal mean emigrant density (mean VIR) and coefficient of variation of emigrant density (CV VIR) to identify areas of consistently-high emigrant density. Radars provided direct comprehensive observations of the spatio-temporal patterns of stopover use of migrating birds across nearly a quarter of the land area within the state of North Carolina. ","tags":["migration radar nc spring"],"snippet":"This dataset contains classified bird stopover density information based on weather surveillance radar data from spring (2000-2003 and 2013-2015).","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-83.17561707983384,33.43359122453189],[-76.20808777